2. THE TURN PER AXIS LINK AND THE FLIGHT'S ACCUMULATOR (the row's two rates)
   the turn: at a Link crossed on the axis a the phase turns by_drive(acc_turn, |p_a| N, h) steps: on a heading |p| N / h = 14080 / 1024 = 13.75 steps per Link; de Broglie's wavelength h / p = 4.6545 Links (the photon world's 4.654)
   the flight: the accumulator's rate 2 |p_D|_1 against the wall 2 E'_D, started at E'_D (today's convention, rate 2 S_1 Q against 2 T_D at the half): the photon case E'_0 = 0 with p = Q D gives the rate 2 S_1 Q and the wall 2 isqrt(3 Q^2 |D|^2) = 2 T_D to the integer, one primitive for every row
   the bounds: E'^2 = 16916769 < 2^62; the turn's numerator |p_a| N <= 14080 and the accumulator below h + |p_a| N; the phase-count vectors of the click as today

3. WHAT THE CLICK PLACES, AND THE BOOKS
   the openings re-release an arriving row of amount w as 1327 rows of amounts w a_i (the weights 123 to 5619, the sum 783863) with the multiplicity m x A, A = sum a_i^2 = 714364777: the copies of one quantum over the fan, as the photon's
   at the click the chosen row's direction D gives the momentum p_D and the content placed is ONE quantum, M = 64 (the family's quantum per unit of the birth's amount 1), whatever the amplitude weight w a_i of the chosen row; the rest of the record's units are cancelled as the photon's are (the books: initial + released = current + escaped + absorbed + cancelled)
   the recoil at a re-release: the wall takes p_D' - p_D per re-emitted row on its own momentum (fixed: no step), as it takes the photon's; the lamp takes -p_D per row born
   the lamp's budget: 4096 births x 5 rows x 64 = 1310720 units of content at the births; the lamp's amount 1073741824 (content 68719476736) holds it 52429 times over

4. THE PIN'S ARRIVALS WITH THE LAMP-TO-OPENING FLIGHT COUNTED (section 23.3 counts from the opening) [SUPERSEDED by the round-2 map's B: the leg below is the heading's row, which hits the stop at (7, 60); the diagonals reach the openings at 139]
   the centre pixel 60: the paths from the openings 44.28 and 44.28 Links, 828 and 828 intervals at the pace 0.05349 (section 23.3's numbers); the lamp at x = 2 to the opening at x = 8: 6 Links more, 112 intervals (the photon's 10), so the first click at the tick about 941 to 941
   the first-fringe pixel 36.7: the paths from the openings 47.65 and 52.32 Links, 891 and 978 intervals at the pace 0.05349 (section 23.3's numbers); the lamp at x = 2 to the opening at x = 8: 6 Links more, 112 intervals (the photon's 10), so the first click at the tick about 1004 to 1091
   the last birth at 4096 arrives by about 4096 + 112 + 978 = 5186: the run needs about 5250 intervals (section 23.3's 5100 counted from the opening)

5. THE HOST COST AGAINST slits_huygens (host numbers)
   a row lives from its birth to its click about 86 intervals for the photon and 940 for the massive row (10.9 times), so with a birth per interval the rows in flight at once are 10.9 times slits_huygens' and the work per interval with them
   slits_huygens ran 4300 intervals in 1334 s (0.31 s per interval); slits_matter at 4096 births and about 5250 intervals: about 4.9 hours; at 1024 births (the wheel [633, 1024], the golden rate at W = 1024) and about 2200 intervals: about 2.1 hours; the records in proportion
